        detail:
          'Holden buys the red hunting hat in New York for a dollar on the morning he loses the fencing team’s equipment on the subway, and he wears it backward, indoors, at the least appropriate moments. It marks him as deliberately separate, which is why he keeps taking it off whenever he might be seen by someone whose opinion frightens him. When Phoebe later sets it on his head in the rain at the carousel, the shield turns into a gift, and that small exchange is as close to a resolution as the novel offers.',
